    "id": "french-charlotte-aux-framboises",
    "category": "french",
    "title": "Charlotte aux Framboises",
    "chineseTitle": null,
    "contributor": "Jeanne Tahnk",
    "occasion": "French Cooking by Jacqueline Hill (Jeanne Tahnk's Gourmet Kitchen)",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Ingredients",
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          "Biscuits a la cuiller (enough to line your mold)",
          "1/2 lb sugar",
          "1/2 lb unsalted butter",
          "1/2 lb powdered almonds",
          "1 cup Cointreau",
          "1 1/2 lbs raspberries (use frozen ones and reserve the juice)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Coulis de Framboise (raspberry sauce)",
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          "juice of the raspberries",
          "5 Tbsps sugar",
          "1/2 cup raspberry brandy"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": null,
        "type": "steps",
        "items": [
          "Soak the biscuits in Cointreau.",
          "Line the bottom and the sides of the mold with the biscuits.",
          "In a mixer, beat the sugar, butter, almonds and half the Cointreau to form a cream.",
          "Fill the mold alternately with a layer of almond cream, a layer of biscuits and a layer of raspberries. Finish with a layer of biscuits.",
          "Refrigerate for 3 hours and put weight on the top of the mold so all the ingredients mix well.",
          "Serve with a coulis de framboises: boil together for a few minutes the juice of the raspberries, 5 Tbsps sugar and 1/2 cup raspberry brandy. Let cool and serve separately in a sauce boat."
        ]
      }
    ],
