    "id": "french-sauce-hollandaise",
    "category": "french",
    "title": "Sauce Hollandaise",
    "chineseTitle": null,
    "contributor": "Jacqueline Hill",
    "occasion": null,
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Ingredients",
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          "4 Tbs milk",
          "1 ts. arrowroot (or cornstarch)",
          "3 egg yolks",
          "juice of 1 lemon",
          "1/2 lb clarified, melted butter",
          "salt and pepper"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": null,
        "type": "steps",
        "items": [
          "Off heat - In a \"bain marie\" sauce pan, mix the arrowroot with the milk, the egg yolks, 4 Tbs of melted butter, lemon juice, salt and pepper.",
          "Heat on - Let this mixture get warm, stirring all the time. Then add the melted butter little by little, always whipping the mixture.",
          "Optional: add 3-4 Tbs whipped cream just before serving (it is then called \"sauce mousseline\")"
        ]
      }
    ],
