    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Ingredients",
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          "3 grapefruit",
          "6 Tablespoons chutney",
          "1/4 cup brandy"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": null,
        "type": "steps",
        "items": [
          "Cut grapefruit in half and remove the center membrane and any seeds. Loosen each section with a grapefruit knife. Place halves in a baking dish with a rim, not a baking sheet.",
          "Spread 1 Tablespoon of chutney over each grapefruit half. Then sprinkle each with 2 teaspoons of brandy. Some brandy will dribble into the pan, but it doesn't matter.",
          "Just before serving, place grapefruit under hot broiler for 5 minutes."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": null,
        "type": "text",
        "items": [
          "To serve - Place each grapefruit half on an individual dish and spoon over it some of the juices that have collected in the pan.",
          "The grapefruit can be cut, spread with chutney and sprinkled with brandy well in advance. Refrigerate if kept more than 2 or 3 hours. Broil at serving time, allowing an extra 2 minutes if the grapefruit has not been brought back to room temperature."
        ]
      }
    ],
