    "id": "mexican-beef-enchiladas-with-sour-cream",
    "category": "mexican",
    "title": "Beef Enchiladas with Sour Cream",
    "chineseTitle": null,
    "contributor": "Jeanne Tahnk",
    "occasion": null,
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Sauce",
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          "1 sm. can enchilada sauce",
          "14 oz. (approx.) chicken or beef broth",
          "1/4 c. flour plus oil for roux",
          "1/4 tsp. garlic powder",
          "salt",
          "pinch of oregano"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Sauce - To Prepare",
        "type": "steps",
        "items": [
          "Saute flour in hot oil. Add sauce & broth while stirring to keep smooth. Add spices & salt. Simmer for 15-20 min."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Filling",
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          "1 1/2 lbs. beef chuck or round",
          "1 clove garlic in cooking water",
          "pinch of oregano",
          "pinch of cumin"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Filling - To Prepare",
        "type": "steps",
        "items": [
          "Simmer until fork tender, about 1 1/2 hours. Drain meat. Shred when cool enough to handle. Add seasonings."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Tortillas",
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          "1 doz. corn tortillas, fresh or frozen",
          "lard or oil for frying",
          "2 c. grated longhorn cheese (approx.)",
          "sour cream",
          "chopped green onions"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Tortillas - To Prepare",
        "type": "steps",
        "items": [
          "Follow pkg. direction to thaw. Place tortillas in hot fat only long enough to soften. Drain. *Toppings."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Assembly",
        "type": "steps",
        "items": [
          "Dip tortillas one at a time into warm sauce. Drain. Stuff about 2 T. filling into each tortilla and roll up. Place in oven-proof flat dish. Pour remaining sauce over enchiladas. Sprinkle cheese over sauce and bake until hot and cheese melts, about 20 min. Remove from oven. Drop dollops of sour cream on top & add green onions. Oven Temp. 350 degrees. Makes 1 doz."
        ]
      }
    ],
