window.ABOUT = {
  "name": "Jeanne Tahnk",
  "paragraphs": [
    "Born in Taiwan, Republic of China, on the beautiful island of Formosa, Jeanne always dreamed of coming to America. By wiggling her nose, working hard, and believing everything she desired would come her way — from her favorite TV show, I Dream of Jeannie, to the present day — Jeanne Tahnk has lived a beautiful, humble life full of many talents and successful careers. She is mother to two wonderful sons, grandmother to six, a friend, and an entrepreneur.",
    "In her lifetime she has gone from fashion designer to cooking master, from competitive dancer to farmer and canner — living a colorful life without regret. Jeanne has always loved dressing in amazing fashion, and since so many people admired what she wore, she and her mother started a fashion company when she was just 18 years old. Jeanne designed and promoted the line while her mother handled production, leading a team of models across the cities of Taiwan.",
    "In 1969, Jeanne followed her heart to America, leaving her very successful fashion business behind for her family to maintain — today, that business runs more than 500 stores. In 1971, she began sharing her love of cooking by starting a cooking school and TV show with local channels, and catering to large organizations and businesses such as MIT, Harvard, the JFK Library, and other cultural events. At the height of her success, she opened the famous Victorian Pink House in Winchester, Massachusetts, naming it Jeanne's Restaurant and Catering. Jeanne taught and catered to over 5,000 students, and to this day people still cook from her amazing recipes.",
    "Did you know Jeanne loves to dance? She began dancing and training in ballet at just three years old, and has competed in numerous USA and international ballroom competitions. Jeanne and her partner trained for 12 years in ballroom dancing, winning numerous gold medals. She is especially fond of the Argentine tango, hula, and salsa.",
    "After settling in Connecticut, Jeanne developed a love of farming and canning, growing and preserving vegetables, herbs, and other produce. She's locally known as the \"Tomato Queen\" from her years running the farm stand at Indian Neck. She has also entered numerous competitions, including the famous annual Durham Fair in Durham, CT — in 2017 and 2018 she won dozens of prize ribbons for her sauces and her displays of vegetables and produce. But the most important win for her is being able to teach and share her recipes, so others can enjoy cooking as much as she does.",
    "The date on the calendar means nothing to Jeanne — she celebrates life, not another birthday. As Jeanne says: \"Life is to be celebrated in such a beautiful way while being surrounded by family and lovely friends. Life has a lot of ups and downs, but you must learn to appreciate every day as it comes. If I was to go today, I can honestly say I lived with no regrets — I am able to do what I love every day.\""
  ]
};

